          "answers": ["$= -\\frac{3}{2}$", "$= 0$", "$= -4$", "$= \\frac{2}{7}$"]
        },
        {
          "q": "If $f(x) = 3x - 7$ and $f(a) = 11$, find the value of $a$.",
          "answer": "$3a - 7 = 11$, so $3a = 18$ and $a = 6$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Identifying functions",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Determine whether each equation defines $y$ as a function of $x$:",
          "parts": ["$y = 2x + 1$", "$x = y^2$", "$y = |x|$", "$x^2 + y^2 = 9$"],
          "cols": 2,
          "answers": [
            "Yes — one output for each input.",
            "No — e.g. $x = 4$ gives $y = 2$ or $y = -2$.",
            "Yes — one output for each input.",
            "No — a circle fails the vertical line test."
          ]
        },
        {
          "q": "Explain how the vertical line test is used to decide whether a graph represents a function.",
          "answer": "If every vertical line crosses the graph at most once, each input $x$ has at most one output $y$, so the graph represents a function. If any vertical line crosses the graph more than once, it is not a function."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Combining functions",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Let $f(x) = x^2 + 1$ and $g(x) = 2x - 3$. Find:",
          "parts": ["$(f + g)(x)$", "$(f - g)(x)$", "$(f \\cdot g)(2)$", "$(f \\circ g)(1)$"],
          "cols": 2,
          "answers": ["$= x^2 + 2x - 2$", "$= x^2 - 2x + 4$", "$= 5 \\cdot 1 = 5$", "$= f(-1) = 2$"]
        },
        {
          "q": "A tutoring center charges a one-time registration fee plus an hourly rate, modeled by $C(n) = 250 + 45n$ riyals for $n$ hours of tutoring.",
          "parts": [
            "Interpret the value $C(0)$ in context.",
            "Find $C(12)$.",
            "Solve $C(n) = 925$ and interpret your answer."
          ],
          "cols": 1,
          "answers": [
            "$C(0) = 250$: the registration fee alone, before any tutoring hours.",
            "$C(12) = 250 + 540 = 790$ riyals.",
            "$45n = 675$, so $n = 15$: a total cost of 925 riyals buys 15 hours of tutoring."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
